      "id": "origins-earth-human-history-s063-p00808",
      "source_en": "But their ships had returned with holds full of cinnamon, cloves, ginger, nutmeg, pepper, and rubies, whereas Columbus' first expedition had found little of any worth. So although it was Columbus' eight-month expedition of 1492 that is most remembered today, in many ways da Gama's 1497 voyage was far more impressive. He had discovered what Columbus set out, but failed, to find: the sea route to the riches of the East.",
